EUROPEAN UNION PUBLIC LICENCE v. 1.2
EUPL – European Union Public Licence

The European Union Public Licence ("EUPL") is a Free and Open Source Software (FOSS) licence.
It can be used by any licensor, for any kind of software, independently of the applicable copyright
and/or neighbouring rights. The EUPL is suitable in particular when the licensed software is
distributed in several versions (e.g. source code and object code) and where common licencing
under several different versions of the same software is desired.

The EUPL was created in accordance with the Directive 2009/24/EC of the European Parliament
and of the Council of 23 April 2009 on the legal protection of computer programs, as amended,
and is compliant with the Open Source Definition (OSD) as maintained by the Open Source Initiative
(OSI). It is also compatible with the GNU General Public License (GPL) version 2 and later.

The full text of the EUPL v. 1.2 is available in all official EU languages at:
  https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32017D0863

